            <div xml:id="d734">

                <pb facs="1019" n="893" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg893"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/504a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-12-27T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 27,
                                1924—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>317. Department’s No. 308, December 9, 4 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d734-f1"/>
                    Colonel Manton Davis, Assistant General Attorney, Radio Corporation, will sail
                    for China at an early date to assist Barnes Moss in negotiations. It is;
                    understood Moss has sailed, or is about to sail, for China.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
